(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["NumericalArray", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"0337f627-b105-4244-93f4-90cbe1860dad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"NumericalArray", "[", "data", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"fcd872d0-bc83-0b4a-a185-6803d6471e0f"],
 " ",
 "represents an array with the explicit entries data, whose value domain is \
inferred."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"e9bca752-0dc5-3645-b381-31649fcf299b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"NumericalArray", "[", 
    RowBox[{"data", ",", " ", "dom"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"8feb33e3-1f80-234d-a7ce-f1bf86d7e244"],
 " ",
 "declares the value domain to be dom."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"39e3f753-b691-bb48-8daf-83af0283afa6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"NumericalArray", "[", 
    RowBox[{"data", ",", " ", "dom", ",", " ", "sym"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]],
   "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"cea5dc90-b4a7-8941-b1e5-d5f458cc11c0"],
 " ",
 "additionally declares the index symmetry sym."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"939cc505-f3fa-bb4c-9f6f-c49f6666a12e"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"f419198c-1105-3f4e-8749-2daa3eebb899"],

Cell["\<\
The entries data must form a rectangular array. A ragged list is not one.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a06335c8-81ba-034a-9ab8-c15fb1717755"],

Cell["\<\
A scalar is accepted as the array of order zero. It has no indices and a \
single entry, and it is what a full contraction leaves behind and what \
multiplies an array entry by entry, so scalar multiplication is nothing but \
ArrayTimes with a 0-array.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c26167bf-662a-cc49-91c2-0b5936b28ed4"],

Cell["\<\
The recognized value domains are \"Boolean\", \"Integer\", \"Rational\", \
\"Real\" and \"Complex\", together with FiniteField[p, n] for the elements of \
a finite field.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"575a6656-5c58-c845-b57d-f3664796c2b2"],

Cell["\<\
When the domain is omitted, or given as Automatic, the narrowest recognized \
domain containing every entry is used. A wider domain may be declared \
instead; a domain that does not contain every entry is rejected with the \
message NumericalArray::entries.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"19e22a43-f1f3-c74c-af0f-d47445ae074e"],

Cell["\<\
The index symmetry sym is one of \"Rigid\" (the default), \"Cyclic\" or \
\"Symmetric\". The spelling is case-insensitive on input, but the stored form \
is always one of the three.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0648bd2d-69b6-1e48-8339-9e8f92c8b2d0"],

Cell["\<\
A declared symmetry is checked against the entries, and rejected with \
NumericalArray::nosym if they are not invariant under the corresponding index \
permutations. Only a regular array can carry a symmetry other than \"Rigid\".\
\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6f24c4b9-d580-294a-844b-5943ae3291d2"],

Cell["\<\
A numerical array displays as a summary box. Normal gives its entries.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6d5cf552-f904-1e4d-b4d5-af69452e1386"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"0d8c0a7a-0f77-5642-9307-bf250155d0c5"],

Cell["\<\
A vector, a matrix and a 3-array. The domain of each is inferred:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"8c616851-d49b-4140-96fc-f11bda5f06c1"],

Cell["\<\
{NumericalArray[{1, 2, 3}], NumericalArray[{{1, 2}, {3, 4}}],
 NumericalArray[Array[#1 + #2 + #3 &, {2, 2, 2}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f4f5309c-4c44-f84a-b9a1-24f950208d83"],

